#====================================================================
# DRAFT-kea-hook-ping-check-3.0.3-ohos-storage-symlink-denial-soname
# — OHOS /storage 沙箱拒绝符号链接：meson 版本化 soname 的物化修法，
#   含 0 字节落盘瞬时异常的自愈与 dlopen 闭包兜底（OHOS/kea-hook-ping-check 3.0.3 实测）
# 触发事件: kea-hook-ping-check 3.0.3 适配（真机 meson test 两套件 exit 127 全败）
# 路径: Path B（知识库扩展）
# 与已有条目关系: E492 覆盖了「meson 版本化库在 OHOS 不暴露别名 → 物化」的主干
#   （zix 0.8.1，2026-08-25 入库）；本条目在其之上的增量 = ①根因钉到文件系统层
#   （ln -s → EPERM，find -type l 计数为 0）②package 产物 0 字节落盘瞬时异常的自愈
#   ③test_package 对包内全部运行库逐个 dlopen(RTLD_NOW) 的闭包兜底
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-kea-hook-ping-check-3.0.3-ohos-storage-symlink-denial-soname
trigger_tool:           meson|conan|ldso
phase:                  testing|packaging|runtime
error_signature: "Error loading shared library libkea-.*so\.\d+:|Error relocating.*symbol not found|exit status 127.*meson test|ln -s.*Permission denied"
root_cause: "The HarmonyOS PC /storage sandbox denies symlink creation at the filesystem level (ln -s -> Permission denied, find -type l returns 0 in a fresh tree). Meson shared_library() with version: 'N.M.K' publishes the soname libX.so.N ONLY as a symlink to the real libX.so.N.M.K file, so on OHOS the soname-name file never exists. Any loader lookup by NEEDED name (the meson test binaries' RPATH/LD_LIBRARY_PATH resolution, and later the packaged hook at dlopen time) then fails with 'Error loading shared library libX.so.N:' which cascades into 'Error relocating ... symbol not found' for the binary's own symbols. A recipe whose build() never runs meson test and whose package() re-creates symlinks defensively (the family template kea-hook-limits) never hits this - the failure surfaces only when the test binaries are actually executed."
rec_approach: "In build(), after meson compile, walk the build tree's library directories and MATERIALIZE each versioned library's soname as a REAL COPY: for every file libX.so.N.M.K (split on '.', len>=4, parts[1]=='so', parts[2]/[3] digits), copyfile it to libX.so.N in the same directory, skipping if the name already exists or is a symlink (idempotent, and on normal Linux hosts where meson already created the symlink the copy is skipped so there is exactly one physical file per name). Both the meson test binaries (which get LD_LIBRARY_PATH with all build dirs) and the package() walk (startswith '{lib}.so.') then see the soname files. Also add a defensive post-copy re-check in package(): any packaged runtime library that landed as a 0-byte file gets re-copied from the build tree with a WARNING log (a transient OHOS /storage write-back glitch zeroed package sonames once on the device), and make the test_package load every packaged library with dlopen(RTLD_NOW) so the closure is verified end to end."
match_keywords: ["soname symlink", "storage sandbox symlink denial", "Error loading shared library", "Error relocating", "exit status 127", "meson version shared library", "libkea", "materialize soname", "copyfile fallback", "0-byte package file", "dlopen closure"]
error_excerpt: "meson test: Error loading shared library libkea-dhcpsrv.so.131: (needed by .../dhcp-ping-check-tests) | Error relocating .../dhcp-ping-check-tests: _ZNK3isc9Exception4whatEv: symbol not found | test_package: dlopen(.../libdhcp_ping_check.so) failed: Error loading shared library libkea-dhcpsrv.so.131"
severity:               2
category:               meson, symlink, packaging, runtime, testing, portability, ohos, filesystem
similar_to:             E492
last_updated: 2026-09-27
